## 5. Validation Checklist

Before trusting your measurements:
- [ ] **Variance Check:** Run the same fight 10 times. If windup frames vary, you're measuring wrong (should be deterministic).
- [ ] **AS Scaling Check:** Double attack speed. Windup time should halve. If it doesn't, you're measuring total animation instead of windup.
- [ ] **Range Check:** RFC (Rapid Firecannon) adds +1 range. If walk speed changes with RFC, you're measuring approach time, not raw speed.

**Red Flags:**
- If you measure a windup of exactly 0.0s, you're detecting the damage frame, not the start of the animation.
- If walk speed differs between melee and ranged units, verify in data files—some units have different base speeds.

**Bottom Line:** You are building a deterministic discrete event simulation. These timings are your **invariant constants**. If you guess them, your model will drift from reality. Frame-count 5-10 key champions (one melee, one ranged, one caster) to establish your baseline constants, then assume homogeneity within archetypes unless proven otherwise.

